0634276:1R.@pl)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:464]<br />{org:en}<br />Determination of specific gravity is a general preliminary method that characterizes the direction of further investigation of water quality.<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />aoj(:01.@entry,     100151497:02.@topic)<br />aoj(301099951:0J,     107512147:0S)<br />mod:01(106197215:2J.@def,     100633864:34)<br />aoj:01(300878086:1D,     105660268:1P.@entry.@indef)<br />mod:01(104723816:3R,     107935504:3L)<br />aoj(301099951:0J,     107512147:0S)<br />mod:01(106197215:2J.@def,     100633864:34)<br />aoj:01(300878086:1D,     105660268:1P.@entry.@indef)<br />mod:01(104723816:3R,     107935504:3L)<br />aoj:01(300487198:15,     105660268:1P.@entry.@indef)<br />mod:01(100633864:34,     300443988:2W)<br />aoj:01(202697950:21,     105660268:1P.@entry.@indef)<br />obj:01(100633864:34,     104723816:3R)<br />obj:01(100633864:34,     104723816:3R)<br />obj:01(202697950:21,     106197215:2J.@def)<br />obj(100151497:02.@topic,     107512147:0S)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:465]<br />{org:en}<br />The determination of the density can also serve for estimation of the isotopic composition of the natural water.<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />aoj(303161531:18.@entry,     100151497:06.@topic.@def)<br />aoj(302902531:20,     103081660:29.@def)<br />obj(105803379:1I,     103081660:29.@def)<br />aoj(302902531:20,     103081660:29.@def)<br />obj(105803379:1I,     103081660:29.@def)<br />man(303161531:18.@entry,     400047534:13)<br />mod(100151497:06.@topic.@def,     104941453:0R.@def)<br />pur(303161531:18.@entry,     105803379:1I)<br />aoj(301335708:2S,     107935504:30.@def)<br />aoj(301335708:2S,     107935504:30.@def)<br />mod(103081660:29.@def,     107935504:30.@def)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:466]<br />{org:en}<br />Determination of admixtures of dissolved and suspended HTM1 matter in water<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />obj(100151497:02.@entry,     102681084:0J.@pl)<br />aoj(301506258:0X,     100020827:1Q)<br />aoj(301506258:0X,     100020827:1Q)<br />plc(100020827:1Q,     107935504:20)<br />mod(102681084:0J.@pl,     100020827:1Q)<br />aoj(302351692:1B,     100020827:1Q)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:467]<br />{org:en}<br />The total content of the admixtures of dissolved and suspended matter is determined by the evaporation of the sample at HTM1 to constant weight and by weighing the residue obtained.<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />obj(200699815:23.@entry,     105809192:0C.@topic.@def)<br />aoj(200699815:23.@entry,     :02)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:468]<br />{org:en}<br />The determination of the dissolved substances is carried out after filtering water through the paper or membrane filter and also after centrifugation of the water sample and subsequent drying the sample at HTM1 and weighing the obtained residue.<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />obj(202774207:1F.@entry,     100151497:06.@topic.@def)<br />man(202774207:1F.@entry,     :04)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:469]<br />{org:en}<br />The difference of results of the first and second determination makes possible determination of the total amount of dissolved substances in milligrams per liter of water.<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />aoj(200012267:1U.@entry,     104748836:06.@topic.@def)<br />obj(200012267:1U.@entry,     100151497:29)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:470]<br />{org:en}<br />Finally, when it is necessary to determine separately the concentration of inorganic (mineral) admixtures and organic substances in the water sample, the operation of calcinations of the second residue at HTM1 is carried out.<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />man(202774207:5Z.@entry,     600000033:0B)<br />man(202774207:5Z.@entry,     400048138:02)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:471]<br />{org:en}<br />The weighing the third residue makes possible determination of the amount of organic substances burning at the calcinations in the air atmosphere as the weight difference between the second and third residues