ing example, in the history of Rome, of civic virtue and the conscientious performance of unwavering duty.<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />aoj(105820620:0N.@entry.@indef,     600000021:02.@topic)<br />and:01(100047106:2P.@entry.@def,     104847298:1W.@def)<br />aoj(300580805:0B,     105820620:0N.@entry.@indef)<br />aoj(105820620:0N.@entry.@indef,     600000021:02.@topic)<br />and:01(100047106:2P.@entry.@def,     104847298:1W.@def)<br />aoj(300580805:0B,     105820620:0N.@entry.@indef)<br />aoj:01(303163862:34,     100719494:3F)<br />plc(105820620:0N.@entry.@indef,     106119729:13.@def)<br />aoj:01(300310138:2B,     100047106:2P.@entry.@def)<br />mod(105820620:0N.@entry.@indef,     :01.@entry)<br />mod(105820620:0N.@entry.@indef,     :01.@entry)<br />mod:01(100047106:2P.@entry.@def,     100719494:3F)<br />mod(106119729:13.@def,     500002215:1E)<br />mod:01(104847298:1W.@def,     302697329:1Q)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:1817]<br />{org:en}<br />In order to provide a record, both for his own use and also more widely throughout the Empire, he compiled this book, HTM1 De Aquis HTM2 containing the results of the program he had laid down for himself at the outset of his work.<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />man(201627105:2Z.@entry.@past,     600000044:05)<br />obj(201544692:5B.@past.@complete,     100551215:4W.@def)<br />man:01(400099341:1X,     400047534:1S)<br />man(:01,     600000074:13)<br />obj(600000810:5X,     100575741:6I)<br />obj(200406963:0H,     100047745:0R.@indef)<br />obj(201627105:2Z.@entry.@past,     102870092:3D)<br />pur(201544692:5B.@past.@complete,     600000669:5P)<br />mod:01(100947128:1K,     301768724:1G)<br />man(201627105:2Z.@entry.@past,     600000044:05)<br />obj(201544692:5B.@past.@complete,     100551215:4W.@def)<br />man:01(400099341:1X,     400047534:1S)<br />man(:01,     600000074:13)<br />obj(600000810:5X,     100575741:6I)<br />obj(200406963:0H,     100047745:0R.@indef)<br />obj(201627105:2Z.@entry.@past,     102870092:3D)<br />pur(20