tions of the atmosphere and the ground as it strongly absorbs the long-wave infrared radiation, which is emitted by the Earth's surface.<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />rsn(105798863:1C.@entry.@pl,     200395698:2Z)<br />obj(200395698:2Z,     101252918:3U.@def)<br />mod(105798863:1C.@entry.@pl,     105725527:17)<br />agt(200105333:4E,     115690588:4T.@def)<br />aoj(301275562:0T,     105798863:1C.@entry.@pl)<br />mod(101252918:3U.@def,     111507511:3B)<br />rsn(105798863:1C.@entry.@pl,     200395698:2Z)<br />obj(200395698:2Z,     101252918:3U.@def)<br />mod(105798863:1C.@entry.@pl,     105725527:17)<br />agt(200105333:4E,     115690588:4T.@def)<br />aoj(301275562:0T,     105798863:1C.@entry.@pl)<br />mod(101252918:3U.@def,     111507511:3B)<br />mod(115055633:0C,     107935504:06)<br />obj(105798863:1C.@entry.@pl,     :01:01)<br />obj(200105333:4E,     101252918:3U.@def)<br />mod(105809192:0I.@topic.@def,     115055633:0C)<br />aoj(105798863:1C.@entry.@pl,     105809192:0I.@topic.@def)<br />man(200395698:2Z,     400177289:2Q)<br />aoj(105798863:1C.@entry.@pl,     105809192:0I.@topic.@def)<br />man(200395698:2Z,     400177289:2Q)<br />and:01(103462594:2D.@entry.@def,     108499057:1U.@def)<br />aoj(303162572:13,     105798863:1C.@entry.@pl)<br />aoj(302517999:3L,     101252918:3U.@def)<br />agt(200395698:2Z,     600000016:2N)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:3627]<br />{org:en}<br />In its turn, the water vapor itself emits the infrared radiation, larger part of that again goes to the surface.<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />plc(200105333:12.@entry,     100292599:09)<br />mod(115055633:0P.@topic.@emphasis.@def,     107935504:0J)<br />obj(200359916:2M,     103892891:23)<br />pof(103892891:23,     101252918:1L.@def)<br />plc(200105333:12.@entry,     100292599:09)<br />mod(115055633:0P.@topic.@emphasis.@def,     107935504:0J)<br />obj(200359916:2M,     103892891:23)<br />pof(103892891:23,     101252918:1L.@def)<br />gol(200359916:2M,     104362025:2Y.@def)<br />obj(20010533