opic)<br />aoj(303162367:08,     103384535:0I.@entry)<br />aoj(103384535:0I.@entry,     600000016:02.@topic)<br />aoj(303162367:08,     103384535:0I.@entry)<br />cnt(103384535:0I.@entry,     HTM1:0P.@parenthesis)<br />mod(103384535:0I.@entry,     114648100:0Z)<br />mod(103384535:0I.@entry,     114648100:0Z)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:3638]<br />{org:en}<br />It is formed in layers from 15 up to 70 km and absorbs ultraviolet radiation with the wavelengths from 0.15 to 0.29 micrometers ( HTM1 ).<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />and(200395698:1D.@entry,     200144850:08)<br />obj(200144850:08,     600000016:02.@topic)<br />obj(600000019:27,     105086269:2G.@def.@pl)<br />qua(115669024:16,     &quot;70&quot;:13)<br />aoj(600000019:27,     101252918:1X)<br />frm(101463259:0I.@pl,     &quot;15&quot;:0U)<br />and(200395698:1D.@entry,     200144850:08)<br />obj(200144850:08,     600000016:02.@topic)<br />obj(600000019:27,     105086269:2G.@def.@pl)<br />qua(115669024:16,     &quot;70&quot;:13)<br />aoj(600000019:27,     101252918:1X)<br />frm(101463259:0I.@pl,     &quot;15&quot;:0U)<br />qua(103759661:3A.@pl,     :01:01)<br />obj(200395698:1D.@entry,     101252918:1X)<br />aoj(600000086:0X,     101463259:0I.@pl)<br />cnt(103759661:3A.@pl,     HTM1:3O.@parenthesis)<br />agt(200395698:1D.@entry,     600000016:02.@topic)<br />plc(200144850:08,     101463259:0I.@pl)<br />agt(200395698:1D.@entry,     600000016:02.@topic)<br />plc(200144850:08,     101463259:0I.@pl)<br />frm(105086269:2G.@def.@pl,     103759661:3A.@pl)<br />aoj(302518601:1L,     101252918:1X)<br />obj(600000086:0X,     115669024:16)<br />fmt:01(&quot;0.29&quot;:35.@entry,     &quot;0.115&quot;:2X)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:3639]<br />{org:en}<br />Absorbing one quantum of the ultraviolet radiation, a part of two-atomic molecules of oxygen dissociates into atoms, and some of them join the remaining oxygen molecules and, thus, form triatomic molecules of ozone.<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />and(:01.@en