l)<br />aoj(301506258:0M,     103584829:0W.@topic.@def)<br />man(301731351:2Q.@entry,     600000023:2Y)<br />mod(103584829:0W.@topic.@def,     600000011:0E)<br />aoj(301731351:2Q.@entry,     103584829:0W.@topic.@def)<br />plc(103584829:0W.@topic.@def,     115691626:14)<br />plc(103584829:0W.@topic.@def,     115691626:14)<br />mod(105717342:35.@def.@pl,     103584829:3N)<br />aoj(600000862:1N,     115691626:14)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:11021]<br />{org:en}<br />Thus, the first step involves oxidation, which causes the destruction of complex compounds and the further transformation of HTM1 into HTM2 , followed by separation of the iron compounds from the water.<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />man(200401538:0N.@entry,     600000141:02)<br />obj:01(100217014:1R.@def,     115690892:26.@pl)<br />obj(200150776:4D,     :01)<br />mod(100285557:0I.@def,     &quot;1&quot;:0C.@ordinal)<br />aoj(201645601:1D,     113530408:0W)<br />obj(100383606:4S,     103081859:5F.@def.@pl)<br />man(200401538:0N.@entry,     600000141:02)<br />obj:01(100217014:1R.@def,     115690892:26.@pl)<br />obj(200150776:4D,     :01)<br />mod(100285557:0I.@def,     &quot;1&quot;:0C.@ordinal)<br />aoj(201645601:1D,     113530408:0W)<br />obj(100383606:4S,     103081859:5F.@def.@pl)<br />obj:01(100398704:3B.@entry.@def,     HTM1:3T)<br />obj(200401538:0N.@entry,     113530408:0W)<br />frm(100383606:4S,     107935504:62.@def)<br />and:01(100398704:3B.@entry.@def,     100217014:1R.@def)<br />aoj(200401538:0N.@entry,     100285557:0I.@def)<br />gol(200150776:4D,     100383606:4S)<br />gol:01(100398704:3B.@entry.@def,     HTM2:47)<br />gol(200150776:4D,     100383606:4S)<br />gol:01(100398704:3B.@entry.@def,     HTM2:47)<br />obj(201645601:1D,     :01)<br />mod(103081859:5F.@def.@pl,     103584829:5A)<br />aoj:01(300443988:33,     100398704:3B.@entry.@def)<br />{/unl}<br />[/S]<br /><br />[S:11022]<br />{org:en}<br />Iron (III) hydroxide is formed from corresponding salts in aqueous medium at pH values exceeding 3, so further operations usually include the formation of a precipitate of iron hydroxide (which is insoluble) and its subsequent separation by the methods of settlement and filtration described above.<br />{/org}<br />{unl}<br />rsn(600000110:2U,     200144850:0Q.@entry)<br />mod:03(105660268:75.@def.@pl,     :02.@entry)<br />mod(103584829:02,     600000303:08.@parenthesis)<br />aoj(301974451:12,     105717342:1G.@pl)<br />obj:03(114591635:4I.@indef,     114914670:52)<br />and:03(100383606:6N.@entry,     100925207:43.@def)<br />plc(200144850:0Q.@entry,     106254475:1X)<br />man:03(200987071:8D,     600000201:8N)<br />obj(200183879:3O,     :03)<br />aoj:03(300122626:6C,     100383606:6N.@entry)<br />rsn(600000110:2U,     200144850:0Q.@entry)<br />mod:03(105660268:75.@def.@pl,     :02.@entry)<br />mod(103584829:02,     600000303:08.@parenthesis)<br />aoj(301974451:12,     105717342:1G.@pl)<br />obj:03(114591635:4I.@indef,     114914670:52)<br />and:03(100383606:6N.@entry,     100925207:43.@def)<br />plc(200144850:0Q.@entry,     106254475:1X)<br />man:03(200987071:8D,     600000201:8N)<br />obj(200183879:3O,     :03)<br />aoj:03(300122626:6C,     100383606:6N.@entry)<br />obj(202669081:2H.@progress,     &quot;3&quot;:2R)<br />aoj:01(301230728:5M.@entry,     600000120:5D.@topic)<br />plc(200144850:0Q.@entry,     115690400:27.@pl)<br />and:02(100191980:7Y.@entry,     105789089:7J)<br />aoj(200183879:3O,     100409211:35.@pl)<br />aoj(202669081:2H.@progress,     115690400:27.@pl)<br />mod:03(114914670:52,     103584829:4X)<br />mod:03(100383606:6N.@entry,     600000016:68)<br />obj(200144850:0Q.@entry,     114914670:0D.@topic)<br />obj:03(200987071:8D,     :02.@entry)<br />obj(600000110:2U,     200183879:3O)<br />aoj(301355089:1P,     106254475:1X)<br />obj:03(200987071:8D,     :02.@entry)<br />obj(600000110:2U,     200183879:3O)<br />aoj(301355089:1P,     106254475:1X)<br />cnt:03(114914670:52,     :01.@parenthesis)<br />ins:03(100383606:6N.@entry,     10566026